[standards/application/frontend/STD-APP-FE-001-react-application-standards.md#std-fe-015-react-testing-library-for-component-tests]

#### STD-FE-015: React Testing Library for Component Tests

**MUST** use React Testing Library (`@testing-library/react`) for all component tests. Do not use Enzyme or shallow rendering.

**MUST** test components via their rendered output and user interactions — not implementation details (internal state, method calls, or DOM structure that does not affect user-visible behaviour).

```tsx
// ✅ COMPLIANT — tests user-visible behaviour
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';
import { ClaimStatusBadge } from './ClaimStatusBadge';

test('renders Approved status with correct label', () => {
  render(<ClaimStatusBadge status="approved" />);
  expect(screen.getByText('Approved')).toBeInTheDocument();
});

test('calls onDismiss when dismiss button is clicked', async () => {
  const onDismiss = jest.fn();
  render(<ClaimStatusBadge status="approved" onDismiss={onDismiss} />);
  await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /dismiss/i }));
  expect(onDismiss).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
});
```

