#### STD-FE-016: axe-core in Every Component Test

**MUST** include an axe-core assertion in the unit test for every component presented to end users. The test **MUST** assert zero violations. This requirement implements the automated testing gate defined in [PTN-APP-FE-001](../../../patterns/application/frontend/PTN-APP-FE-001-accessible-component-pattern.md) §Acceptance Criteria.

```bash
npm install --save-dev jest-axe
```

```tsx
import { render } from '@testing-library/react';
import { axe, toHaveNoViolations } from 'jest-axe';
import { MemberIdInput } from './MemberIdInput';

expect.extend(toHaveNoViolations);

test('MemberIdInput has no accessibility violations', async () => {
  const { container } = render(<MemberIdInput value="" onChange={() => {}} />);
  expect(await axe(container)).toHaveNoViolations();
});
```

Axe-core **MUST** be configured to target `wcag22aa` rules (see [GUID-APP-ACC-001](../../../strategy/guidance/application/accessibility/GUID-APP-ACC-001-accessible-component-implementation-guidance.md) §5 for full configuration).

